    <main class="privacy-content">

      <section class="privacy-section" id="who-we-are">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-purple">🏢</div>
          <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
        </div>
        <p><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Footmarq</strong> (operating as <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">My_Login</strong>) is a digital identity hub that helps you discover, monitor, and clean up online accounts linked to your email addresses. This service is built and operated by Shivam Kumar.</p>
        <p>This Privacy Policy applies to all services at <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">footmarq.app</strong> and describes how we collect, use, store, and protect your personal information.</p>
        <div class="alert-box">
          <span class="alert-icon">📋</span>
          <span>By creating an account or connecting your Gmail, you agree to the practices described in this policy. If you disagree, please do not use the service.</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" id="what-we-collect">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-blue">📥</div>
          <h2>2. What Data We Collect</h2>
        </div>
        <p>We only collect the minimum data needed to provide the service. Here is a complete, transparent breakdown:</p>
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Category</th><th>What We Store</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Profile</strong></td><td>Name, primary email, profile picture, account creation date</td><td>Identify your account</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Connected Emails</strong></td><td>Email addresses you add, OAuth scopes granted, connection date</td><td>Enable Gmail scanning</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Gmail Metadata</strong></td><td>Sender email, sender name, email subject, received date</td><td>Discover linked services</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Discovered Accounts</strong></td><td>Service name, event type (signup/login), detected date</td><td>Build your account dashboard</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Breach Data</strong></td><td>Which of your emails appeared in known breach databases</td><td>Alert you to compromised accounts</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Security Events</strong></td><td>Sign-in timestamps, device type, IP address</td><td>Protect against unauthorised access</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Scan History</strong></td><td>Scan timestamps, emails processed count (auto-purged after 30 days)</td><td>Track progress, allow resuming</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>OAuth Tokens</strong></td><td>Encrypted Gmail access and refresh tokens</td><td>Authenticate Gmail API calls</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" id="never-collected">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-green">🚫</div>
          <h2>3. What We Never Collect</h2>
        </div>
        <p>We are explicit about what we <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">never</strong> store. These are firm, technical rules — not just policy statements:</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Email body content</strong> — We never read or store the body/text of any email, ever.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Email attachments</strong> — Files attached to your emails are never accessed.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Email thread content</strong> — Full conversation threads are not read or stored.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">CC / BCC headers</strong> — We only read the primary sender and recipient.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Gmail labels or categories</strong> — Your inbox organisation stays private.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Passwords</strong> — We never store or request your passwords for third-party services.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Data sold to third parties</strong> — Your data is never sold, rented, or traded.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Advertising profiles</strong> — We build no advertising or tracking profiles on you.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" id="gmail-access">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-amber">🔑</div>
          <h2>4. Gmail & Google OAuth Access</h2>
        </div>
        <p>This is the most critical section for users who connect Gmail. We follow Google's strictest data handling requirements.</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> We request <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">gmail.readonly</strong> scope only — we can <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">only read</strong> email metadata, nothing else.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> Gmail access is a <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">separate, deliberate step</strong> — you can log in with Google without ever granting Gmail access.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> OAuth tokens are encrypted using <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">AES-256-GCM</strong> before being stored in our database.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> We use Gmail's <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">metadata-only</strong> API format — the most privacy-preserving option available.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> We <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">cannot</strong> send emails on your behalf.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> We <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">cannot</strong> delete your emails.</li>
          <li><span class="no">✕</span> We <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">cannot</strong> manage your Gmail labels or filters.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="alert-box">
          <span class="alert-icon">🔌</span>
          <span>You can revoke Gmail access at any time from <strong>Settings → Privacy</strong>. We immediately call Google's OAuth revocation endpoint and delete all tokens. Your discovered accounts are retained unless you explicitly delete them.</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" id="how-we-use">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-purple">⚙️</div>
          <h2>5. How We Use Your Data</h2>
        </div>
        <p>We use your data for one purpose only: to provide the Footmarq service to you.</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> To <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">discover accounts</strong> linked to your connected email addresses by analysing email metadata.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> To <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">check your emails</strong> against the Have I Been Pwned breach database and alert you to compromises.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> To <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">calculate your security score</strong> based on breach status, risk levels, and 2FA gaps.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> To <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">send notifications</strong> (email only) about scan completion, new breaches, and security alerts.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> To <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">authenticate your sessions</strong> and protect your account from unauthorised access.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not use your data for analytics, A/B testing, marketing, or any purpose outside of directly serving you.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" id="data-security">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-green">🔒</div>
          <h2>6. Data Security</h2>
        </div>
        <p>We implement industry-standard protections across all layers of our infrastructure:</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> All traffic is served over <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">HTTPS/TLS</strong> with HSTS headers enforced.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> OAuth tokens are encrypted at rest using <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">AES-256-GCM</strong> with a server-side encryption key.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> Passwords are hashed using <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">bcrypt</strong> — we never store plaintext passwords.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> Sessions use <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">secure, HTTP-only cookies</strong> — inaccessible to client-side JavaScript.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> Scan logs are <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">automatically purged after 30 days</strong>.</li>
          <li><span class="yes">✓</span> All OAuth flows use <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">CSRF state tokens</strong> to prevent OAuth hijacking attacks.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="alert-box">
          <span class="alert-icon">⚠️</span>
          <span>If you discover a security vulnerability, please contact us at <strong>kumarshivam51238@gmail.com</strong> before public disclosure. We take all reports seriously and will respond within 48 hours.</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" id="your-rights">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-pink">⚖️</div>
          <h2>7. Your Rights (GDPR Art. 15, 17, 20)</h2>
        </div>
        <p>You have the following rights — all built directly into the Footmarq platform under <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Settings → Privacy</strong>:</p>
        <div class="rights-grid">
          <div class="right-card">
            <h4>📤 Export Your Data</h4>
            <p>Download a complete ZIP archive of everything we store — profile, emails, accounts, events, and breaches.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="right-card">
            <h4>🗑️ Delete Scan Logs</h4>
            <p>Purge all scan history and email events while keeping your discovered accounts and profile intact.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="right-card">
            <h4>🔌 Revoke Gmail Access</h4>
            <p>Disconnect Gmail at any time. Tokens are deleted and Google is notified immediately.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="right-card">
            <h4>💀 Delete Account</h4>
            <p>Permanently delete your account and all associated data. All Google tokens are revoked first.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" id="cookies">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-amber">🍪</div>
          <h2>8. Cookies & Sessions</h2>
        </div>
        <p>We use cookies only for essential authentication. We use no tracking, advertising, or analytics cookies.</p>
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>session_token</strong></td><td>Authenticates your login session. HTTP-only, secure, cannot be read by JavaScript.</td><td>Until logout or expiry</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>csrf_token</strong></td><td>Prevents cross-site request forgery attacks on OAuth flows.</td><td>Per-request</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>We do <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">not</strong> use Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, Hotjar, or any third-party tracking scripts.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" id="third-parties">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-blue">🔗</div>
          <h2>9. Third-Party Services</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Footmarq uses the following third-party services strictly to operate the platform. We share no data with any other parties.</p>
        <table class="data-table">
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Service</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Data Shared</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Google OAuth & Gmail API</strong></td><td>Authentication and reading Gmail metadata for account discovery</td><td>Only what you explicitly authorise</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Have I Been Pwned (HIBP)</strong></td><td>Checking if your emails appear in known data breaches</td><td>Your email address (hashed, per HIBP protocol)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>MongoDB</strong></td><td>Encrypted storage of all application data</td><td>All data described in Section 2</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Gmail SMTP (Nodemailer)</strong></td><td>Sending transactional emails — scan summaries, breach alerts, exports</td><td>Your email address and notification content only</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-section" id="contact-privacy">
        <div class="section-icon-title">
          <div class="section-icon icon-purple">📞</div>
          <h2>10. Contact & Privacy Requests</h2>
        </div>
        <p>For privacy-related questions, data requests, or concerns, contact us directly. We aim to respond within <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">48 hours</strong>.</p>
        <div class="contact-box">
          <div class="contact-box-icon">✉️</div>
          <div>
            <h4>Privacy Contact</h4>
            <p>Email: <a href="mailto:kumarshivam51238@gmail.com">kumarshivam51238@gmail.com</a><br>
            Subject line: <em>"Privacy Request — Footmarq"</em></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top:16px;">You may also exercise your rights directly at <strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Settings → Privacy</strong> without needing to contact us.</p>
      </section>

    </main>
  </div>

